# Copy this file to api_key.env (or .env) and uncomment ONE key.
#
# With every line commented there is no AI engine: the dashboard offers only the
# system model, a deterministic local scorer that makes no network calls. The host
# that supplies the key also decides the endpoint and the default model, so
# nothing else has to be set. QWEN_BASE_URL and QWEN_MODEL override either when
# you want a different model or host.

# Gemini: https://aistudio.google.com/api-keys
# Default model: gemini-3.6-flash, through Google's compatible endpoint.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --- Free hosted tiers: no local install, no credit card ---------------------

# Groq — key from the API Keys page at https://console.groq.com
# Free plan: 30 requests/min and, per model, an output-tokens-per-minute cap.
# Default model: openai/gpt-oss-120b, 6 customers per call.
# Measured: that model scored 30/30 SaaS customers at AUC 1.000. Do not switch it
# to the Qwen models on this host — qwen3.6-27b returns an empty generation that
# fails Groq's JSON validation, and qwen3.8-27b needs ~1,900 output tokens for ten
# customers against a 1,000-per-minute cap that refuses the request outright.
# GROQ_API_KEY=

# Hugging Face Inference Providers — fine-grained token from
# https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens/new with "Make calls to Inference
# Providers" enabled. The free plan is a small monthly credit, not a rate limit.
# Default model: openai/gpt-oss-120b:cheapest
# HF_TOKEN=

# OpenRouter — free ":free" models, key from your account settings.
# Default model: openai/gpt-oss-120b:free
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# --- Paid / original host ---------------------------------------------------

# Alibaba Cloud Model Studio (Qwen), the host this platform was built against.
# Default model: qwen-max
# DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=

# --- Any other OpenAI-compatible host ---------------------------------------

# A key with no host of its own needs the endpoint spelled out. Google's Gemini
# free tier works this way:
# AI_API_KEY=
# QWEN_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/
# QWEN_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash

# --- Behaviour --------------------------------------------------------------

# Whether the AI engine is built at all — which engine scores a given run is the
# dashboard's choice, not this file's. auto builds the AI engine when a key
# exists and makes it the default button; mock switches it off even with a key
# present, leaving only the local system model; live requires a key and raises at
# startup if none resolves, so a deployment meant to call a model cannot quietly
# fall back to local scoring.
# QWEN_MODE=auto

# Customers per model call. Defaults to the host's own limit — Groq refuses a
# reply that would exceed 1,000 output tokens a minute, so it defaults to 6, and
# hosts with no such cap default to 10. Lower it if a reply comes back truncated,
# which costs more calls but keeps each one inside the model's output budget.
# BATCH_SIZE=10

# 0 = no cap. A free tier is token-metered, so capping the upload is what keeps
# one analysis inside the daily budget: 100 customers is roughly 27K-40K prompt
# tokens per sector, plus the model's reply. It is also wall-clock — a real
# 100-customer SaaS run on Groq's free plan took about six minutes, and the
# upload request blocks for all of it.
# MAX_ENTITIES=0

# QWEN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120
# QWEN_MAX_RETRIES=4
